00:08:16.949 --> 00:08:18.449
I'm excited, I'm really excited.

00:08:18.449 --> 00:08:19.980
I've not had strawberries like this.

00:08:19.980 --> 00:08:20.813
- Really?

00:08:20.813 --> 00:08:22.005
- They are juicy as.

00:08:22.005 --> 00:08:24.213
- [Rich] It's like an upside
down cheesecake, isn't it?

00:08:24.213 --> 00:08:25.046
- Oh yeah.

00:08:25.046 --> 00:08:25.879
- What is goin' on?

00:08:25.879 --> 00:08:26.712
It's so good.

00:08:26.712 --> 00:08:28.240
- The apricots are so sweet.

00:08:28.240 --> 00:08:29.670
- Everything on steroids.

00:08:29.670 --> 00:08:30.503
(evil laugh)

00:08:30.503 --> 00:08:31.451
A bit of champagne to top it off.

00:08:31.451 --> 00:08:32.583
I'm feeling pretty good.

00:08:32.583 --> 00:08:33.525
(clinking glasses)

00:08:33.525 --> 00:08:34.466
What's a line from a Wes Anderson film.

00:08:34.466 --> 00:08:36.271
I feel like we should end it with like.

00:08:36.271 --> 00:08:38.424
- I don't think I know any.

00:08:38.424 --> 00:08:42.591
Maybe we should make this
bit a bit grainy, zoom out.

00:08:43.935 --> 00:08:45.181
- [Rich] All the places were amazing,

00:08:45.181 --> 00:08:47.249
but which is the most worth it to you?

00:08:47.249 --> 00:08:48.639
- Lucy's was really good,

00:08:48.639 --> 00:08:51.105
but my Worth It winner is, for sure,

00:08:51.105 --> 00:08:52.147
(cash register chimes)

00:08:52.147 --> 00:08:53.371
the Sanderson hotel.

00:08:53.371 --> 00:08:56.462
I can't get over that scotch
egg, it changed my life.

00:08:56.462 --> 00:08:59.365
- Oh yeah, I really liked
Sketch, that was insane.

00:08:59.365 --> 00:09:00.198
I've gotta go with Lucy's.

00:09:00.198 --> 00:09:01.031
(cash register chimes)
- [Ada] Really?

00:09:01.031 --> 00:09:04.265
- Sweet, traditional, I like
that it was a family-run place.

00:09:04.265 --> 00:09:05.098
- [Ada] Yeah.

00:09:05.098 --> 00:09:07.318
- Just felt like a
little, content, old lady.

00:09:07.318 --> 00:09:09.280
Just enjoyin' my afternoon
tea at a tea shop.

00:09:09.280 --> 00:09:10.753
Wait, who is quaint?

00:09:10.753 --> 00:09:11.908
You pointin' at me for quaint?

00:09:11.908 --> 00:09:12.741
- [Multiple Voices] You're quaint.

00:09:12.741 --> 00:09:13.860
- (laughs)
- [Liz] You don't like quaint?

00:09:13.860 --> 00:09:16.582
- No, but for a person
being described as quaint,

00:09:16.582 --> 00:09:17.524
that's crap.

00:09:17.524 --> 00:09:20.074
You're interesting, you're
psychedelic, I'm quaint.

00:09:20.074 --> 00:09:21.657
- I am interestin'.

00:09:24.110 --> 00:09:26.027
(bell)

00:09:27.068 --> 00:09:30.818
(upbeat rhythmic jazz music)

00:09:37.315 --> 00:09:38.400
(swish)

00:09:38.400 --> 00:09:41.233
(creaking hinges)

